00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.370
cluster, an HPC environment,
and that environment

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.820
is managed using something
known as Kubernetes.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.270
So some of you may have
heard of Kubernetes.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:33.430
That's one of these HPC
managers that we support.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.160
If you also use Slurm, we
can support that as well.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.680
Or you can also just run these
tools on a single server.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.630
That's totally fine as well.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.680
But one of the advantages of
using Kubernetes or Slurm is

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.850
you can actually control
this job's CPU and memory

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.780
allocations.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.760
So if you just have
a small job, you

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.010
want to maybe create a plot
or a simple application.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.700
You can keep the CPU
low, keep the memory low,

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:01.120
and that's just great for
managing compute resources.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.270
But if you have a higher
compute, more demanding job,

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:05.660
I can bump that up.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.020
For example, I can
change in memory as well.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:11.440
So really good at
managing resources.

