00:23:51.390 --> 00:23:53.450
We can give you some
more customized URL.

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:59.580
I come down here at content
URL and I can just dash app and hit

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:01.110
Save.

00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:03.263
And now we have
this customized URL

00:24:03.263 --> 00:24:04.680
at the bottom of
the screen, which

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:07.200
we can then share with
the world and anyone

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:10.560
can view this content.

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:13.380
So let's talk about a few of
the other options you have,

00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:15.480
again, as a publisher.

00:24:15.480 --> 00:24:18.570
You have tight control
over this dash application.

00:24:18.570 --> 00:24:21.480
And the next one we'll
go to is runtime.

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:25.020
And this is where you can
control the compute resources

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:28.740
or Python processes
supporting this application.

00:24:28.740 --> 00:24:30.930
If it's a real
lightweight application

00:24:30.930 --> 00:24:33.180
doesn't require a
lot of compute power,

00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:34.480
you can keep it very low.

00:24:34.480 --> 00:24:36.390
But if you have an
application that's

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:39.240
maybe crunching some
large data or training

00:24:39.240 --> 00:24:41.190
a model, for example,
you might want

00:24:41.190 --> 00:24:44.430
to allocate some additional
Python processes.

00:24:44.430 --> 00:24:47.550
So there are Python processes
supporting this application

00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:49.080
while it's running.

00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:53.070
We can define a minimum number
of processes, a maximum, which

00:24:53.070 --> 00:24:55.470
you can see here set
to three, and then you

00:24:55.470 --> 00:24:57.990
have max connections
per process.

00:24:57.990 --> 00:24:59.910
Now if I share that
link with somebody

00:24:59.910 --> 00:25:03.000
and they click on that link,
they become a connection

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:04.800
to this application.

00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:08.280
So by default here I can
have up to 50 connections

00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:10.830
and up to three processes,
so I could support up

00:25:10.830 --> 00:25:13.740
to 150 concurrent users.

00:25:13.740 --> 00:25:15.750
Now, that may be perfect
for what you need.

00:25:15.750 --> 00:25:18.205
Maybe you want to tweak it
and you can do that again.

00:25:18.205 --> 00:25:19.830
As a publisher, you
don't have to worry

00:25:19.830 --> 00:25:22.410
about your administrators
and talking to them

00:25:22.410 --> 00:25:23.420
and configuring it.

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:25.350
You can do it as a publisher.

00:25:25.350 --> 00:25:26.910
So, for example,
I can come in here

00:25:26.910 --> 00:25:30.990
and I can give it 10 more
additional processes.

00:25:30.990 --> 00:25:32.610
And then in this
configuration, I

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:35.680
can support up to
500 concurrent users.

00:25:35.680 --> 00:25:40.200
So 50 connections per process
and up to 10 processes.

00:25:40.200 --> 00:25:44.490
So again, that's how you can
control it as a publisher.

00:25:44.490 --> 00:25:46.740
A few additional options
here along the top,

00:25:46.740 --> 00:25:48.360
the Scheduling tab.

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:51.430
This actually does not apply
to interactive content.

00:25:51.430 --> 00:25:56.640
So things like dash streamlit,
bokeh or within the R ecosystem

00:25:56.640 --> 00:25:58.240
like Shiny applications.

00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:00.480
So scheduling jobs
doesn't necessarily

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:05.970
apply to interactive content,
but if you are deploying things

00:26:05.970 --> 00:26:09.150
like R Markdown or Jupyter
Notebooks or even quarto

00:26:09.150 --> 00:26:12.330
documents, you can actually
place code in those documents

00:26:12.330 --> 00:26:14.340
and schedule them to run.

00:26:14.340 --> 00:26:15.160
So this is great.

00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:17.490
If you have any recurring
jobs, maybe every morning

00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:20.430
when you come in, you
can actually place them

00:26:20.430 --> 00:26:21.960
into any of those
documents I just

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:25.560
mentioned hosted on Connect and
you can schedule to run however

00:26:25.560 --> 00:26:27.720
frequently you want.

00:26:27.720 --> 00:26:29.940
And then just to round
out the last two here

00:26:29.940 --> 00:26:32.520
tags are just for
organizing your content.

00:26:32.520 --> 00:26:36.570
So if you have maybe a study
or a project you're working on

00:26:36.570 --> 00:26:39.090
and there's a variety of
pieces of content associated

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:41.130
with that project,
you can create a tag

00:26:41.130 --> 00:26:45.190
to help easily organize and pull
up that various content types.

00:26:45.190 --> 00:26:47.850
And the last one here is vars.

00:26:47.850 --> 00:26:51.450
If your content requires some
type of privileged access

00:26:51.450 --> 00:26:54.330
to a database or an
API, for example,

00:26:54.330 --> 00:26:56.610
you can come into the
vars tab right here

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:59.340
and supply that
password or API key.

00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:01.590
So the application
has those credentials

00:27:01.590 --> 00:27:06.500
to access that database
or API, for example.

00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:07.250
All right.

00:27:07.250 --> 00:27:08.760
So that's pretty much it.

00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:11.720
And just to recap again
what we did today,

00:27:11.720 --> 00:27:13.440
we started in Posit Workbench.

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:15.890
We created that vs code session.

00:27:15.890 --> 00:27:17.870
We downloaded the
dash application

00:27:17.870 --> 00:27:20.380
from the jumpstart
example hosted in connect.

00:27:20.380 --> 00:27:22.100
So that stock example.

00:27:22.100 --> 00:27:23.600
And then we went
through the process

00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:26.270
of deploying that application
to Posit connect

00:27:26.270 --> 00:27:27.920
and then sharing
it with the world.

00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:30.890
And as we did that, we
were installing packages

00:27:30.890 --> 00:27:34.850
from our instance of
Posit package manager.

00:27:34.850 --> 00:27:37.062
So hopefully this Posit
team overview was helpful

00:27:37.062 --> 00:27:39.020
and we're just going to
go ahead and open it up

00:27:39.020 --> 00:27:42.350
to any questions from the
audience, general discussion,

00:27:42.350 --> 00:27:45.940
and we'd be happy to answer
any questions anybody has.

